<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Intentionally empty until the paid Apple Developer Program is set up.

  Two entitlements need to land here once a paid provisioning profile is
  available; adding them earlier breaks Personal-Team builds because Xcode
  rejects entitlements the profile doesn't carry:

    1. com.apple.developer.networking.multicast
       Required for iroh / Bonjour LAN peer discovery. Without it, peer
       devices on the same Wi-Fi are invisible to each other and sync is
       manual-pair-only. Requires a separate written application to Apple
       after enrolling — they approve case-by-case for apps with a
       legitimate multicast need (mDNS / Bonjour / iroh discovery is
       the canonical case).

    2. com.apple.developer.icloud-services (optional)
       Required only if we want to pick iCloud Drive roost folders via
       the file picker. Local folders work without it.

  See docs/ios-development.md § 6 and docs/ios-todo.md for the running
  iOS work list. When adding either entitlement, also bump
  ios-todo.md's "Done" section so the project journal stays accurate.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict/>
</plist>
